NAME
    more, less - page output a screen at a time

SYNOPSIS
    more <file>
    <command> | more

DESCRIPTION
    Displays a file (or piped input) one screen at a time. `less` is the same
    program. At each --More-- pause:
        space   next screen
        Enter   one more line
        q       quit
    Ctrl+C aborts. Content is buffered, so a very large source is paged up to
    the buffer size and then truncated.

EXAMPLES
    more manual.txt
    ls -l /bin | more

SEE ALSO
    cat
